  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Ahmet Öngün is a Turkish technology entrepreneur who founded Gantek and co-founded the software business Kron. An electrical and electronics engineering graduate of the University of Wales, he worked in London before leading Gantek as chairman. He also established its academy to teach enterprise computing skills to graduates and IT professionals.",
    "html": "<p>Ahmet Öngün is a Turkish technology entrepreneur who founded Gantek and co-founded the software business Kron. An electrical and electronics engineering graduate of the University of Wales, he worked in London before leading Gantek as chairman. He also established its academy to teach enterprise computing skills to graduates and IT professionals.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 51,
