  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Technology entrepreneur Ahmet Öngün and his friend Erdal Tokcan drove an Anadol in the Beijing–Paris classic-car rally to raise money for university scholarships. Their journey nearly ended in Greece when a collision burst the radiator. They patched it with putty, then Tokcan's son delivered a replacement the following day so they could continue.\n\nThe campaign directed sponsorship income and donations to Turkey's Community Volunteers Foundation, which funded students throughout their university education. Öngün had already won consecutive Turkish historic-rally titles before undertaking the intercontinental event. He and Tokcan finished second in the rally's Classics category.",
    "html": "<p>Technology entrepreneur Ahmet Öngün and his friend Erdal Tokcan drove an Anadol in the Beijing–Paris classic-car rally to raise money for university scholarships. Their journey nearly ended in Greece when a collision burst the radiator. They patched it with putty, then Tokcan's son delivered a replacement the following day so they could continue.</p>\r\n<p>The campaign directed sponsorship income and donations to Turkey's Community Volunteers Foundation, which funded students throughout their university education. Öngün had already won consecutive Turkish historic-rally titles before undertaking the intercontinental event. He and Tokcan finished second in the rally's Classics category.</p>\r\n",
